    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required: on successful owner create, enqueue a welcome notification by emitting \u2014 via a logger named `NOTIFY` \u2014 a line containing the owner id and the memberId.\n\nI made two changes in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n1. **Added a dedicated `NOTIFY` logger** alongside the existing `AUDIT` logger.\n\n2. **Emitted the welcome notification** on successful create. In `addOwner(...)`, after the owner is persisted (and after the existing audit-event emission), it now calls a new `enqueueWelcomeNotification(owner)` helper that logs:\n   ```\n   NOTIFY - Welcome notification: ownerId=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1\n   ```\n   containing both `owner.getId()` and `owner.getMemberId()`.\n\nThis fires only on the successful-create path (after all validation/quota checks pass and the owner is saved), matching the spec's \"on successful create.\" The acceptance test `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` \u2014 which captures the `NOTIFY` logger and asserts a line contains both the owner id and the memberId read back from `GET /api/owners/{id}` \u2014 passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
